==Enemy==
Metal Hippoe is a stronger version of the regular [[Hippoe]]. Its attack rate is faster, and it only takes one damage from non-critical hits. At 100% strength magnification, it has 80 health and two knockbacks. Depending on the stage, it can be either annoying or helpful, which is expanded upon in the lower paragraph.

In some stages, Metal Hippoe can act as an annoying tank, such as in [[Chubby B. Goode]] and [[Prison Destruction]], and other times it can be a help for stalling as you build up long-ranged cats, like in [[Tunafish Trenches]] or [[Archaeology 501: Analysis]].

==Strategy==
While it may seem tough when you first encounter it, quick attackers, such as [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]], [[Mr. (Special Cat)|Mr.]] and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]], are able to easily defeat it due to their quick attack speed. Alternatively, you can use [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]], [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]] or [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]] and hope for a [[Critical Hit]]. [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] absolutely destroys Metal Hippoe due to his very high attack rate. Units with guaranteed Critical chance can help at destroying it quickly, though this may not be necessary given its somewhat weak offense.

Another way is to use its mediocre stats to your advantage. Using slow-attacking units to slowly whittle its health down while you build up a stack of [[Long Distance]] units to use for later. This technique is called "Long-Distance stepping stone" or "LD step stone" for short.

